## Component Composition Pattern

### Creating Variant-Specific Components

When creating preset variants, use simple wrapper pattern:

```typescript
// Base component already handles ref forwarding
const Display = (props: TextBaseProps) => {
  return <Text variant="display" {...props} />
}

const Title = (props: TextBaseProps) => {
  return <Text variant="title" {...props} />
}
```

**Why no forwardRef?**

- Base component already handles ref forwarding
- Wrapper just passes props through
- Simpler, less boilerplate

---

## External Library Integration

### Wrapping External Components

When integrating external libraries (e.g., `react-icons`), use wrapper pattern:

```typescript
const Component = forwardRef<HTMLSpanElement, ComponentProps>(
  ({ name, size = 24, ...restProps }, ref) => {
    const ExternalComponent = componentMap[name]

    return (
      <span
        ref={ref}
        css={(theme: Theme) => getStyles(theme)}
        {...restProps}
      >
        <ExternalComponent size={size} />
      </span>
    )
  }
)
```

**Why wrap with span/div?**

- External components may not support ref
- Apply Emotion styles to container
- Support HTML attributes (className, onClick, etc.)
- Control layout with flexbox

