## Package Dependencies

### Emotion Setup

**Required:**

- `@emotion/react` - Core functionality, css prop

**Optional:**

- `@emotion/styled` - styled-components API (most design systems use only `@emotion/react`)

**Vite Integration:**

```typescript
// vite.config.ts
import tsconfigPaths from 'vite-tsconfig-paths'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    react({ jsxImportSource: '@emotion/react' }),
    tsconfigPaths(), // Auto-reads tsconfig paths
  ],
})
```

---

## Summary Checklist

- [ ] Component types defined in `src/types/components/`
- [ ] Theme type inference setup (no circular references)
- [ ] Props are optional with default values (for forwardRef compatibility)
- [ ] Style logic separated into functions
- [ ] Type assertion `as ComponentType` used
- [ ] Component composition uses simple wrappers (no redundant forwardRef)
- [ ] External libraries wrapped properly for ref and style support
- [ ] Full TypeScript type safety maintained

This pattern is production-tested and used by major Korean tech companies (Toss, Kakao, Daangn).
